{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"UPDATED MEASUREMENTS (2026-07-29) — the problem has MORE THAN DOUBLED while this epic has been tabled. Measured independently today while answering an operator question about repo size; the analysis re-derived this epic's finding #3 from scratch, which is strong corroboration.\n\n| | this epic's original measurement | today |\n|---|---|---|\n| tickets store | ~443 MB | **1.03 GiB packed** |\n| .bridge_state total | ~375 MB (85%%) | **942.5 MB (91%%)** |\n| bindings.json | 219 MB / ~987 versions | **739.8 MB / 3,009 versions** (avg 252 KB packed) |\n| prev_snapshot.json | 155 MB / ~4,450 versions | **202.7 MB / 5,151 versions** (avg 40 KB) |\n\nFor contrast, everything else in the pack: ALL real ticket events ~14 MB, REVIEW_RESULT sidecars 24.5 MB, code + everything else 25.9 MB.\n\n## Finding #3 independently re-confirmed, with a sharper number\n\nDiffing two consecutive bindings.json revisions (8c1c4de -> 29dbd53): the file grew only **+2,470 bytes**, and only **1,229 added / 1,166 deleted lines out of 526,487 (0.45%%)**. Of those ~2,395 changed lines, **2,290 are `baseline_advanced_at`** — **96%% of all churn**. The remaining ~69 lines are real change (type, text, last_get_pass). In a single version there are 1,507 occurrences of the field with 230 distinct values, but **1,145 carry the SAME value**, bumped together each pass. It is one logical fact duplicated ~1,145 times, scattered across 18 MB, which is precisely what defeats delta compression.\n\n## Finding #4 (structure) also confirmed\n\nbindings.json holds 1,507 bindings, ~6.4 KB of baseline each. Within baseline: **description 86.4%%** (stored as a full nested ADF dict), status 6.0%%, assignee 3.2%%, priority 3.2%%, summary 1.3%%. baseline is 98.6%% of all per-binding bytes. Matches this epic's '97%% baseline, 86%% description as ADF' exactly.\n\n## One NEW datum that constrains the options\n\nAggressive repack is NOT a lever — I checked delta state directly: **8,157 of 8,165 bridge-state blobs are ALREADY deltified** (avg depth 13.9) and still occupy 940.5 MB; only 8 blobs (1.9 MB) are non-deltified. So there is essentially no delta headroom left in the existing pack, and `git gc`/`repack` can only reclaim ~3.7 MiB of stray tmp_pack garbage plus consolidate 14 packs. That removes 'just repack it' from the option set and makes plan step 2 (the churn guard) the only thing that actually stops the growth without a history rewrite.\n\nRecommendation: the churn guard in plan step 2 is cheap, needs no migration, and alone collapses per-pass churn from ~2,395 changed lines to ~69. Given the doubling, consider un-tabling at least that step independently of the riskier text-normalize/digest/history-reclaim work.\n\nFiled 7f6c-df12-e3dc-4691 before finding this epic; it is a duplicate and is being closed in favour of this one."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785350227617908001,"uuid":"14128f1c-44e0-49d5-a0d1-b1fe98c14777"}